-- Test Description
-- This test ensures that the transmit functionality of the GEM properly 
-- deals with sixteen collisions occurring during the transmission of a frame.  
-- Also, ensures that the GEM can recover buffers after the collisions have occurred.
--
-- Functional Coverage
-- · Ensures that the GEM works properly when a frame is trying to be 
--   transmitted and a total of 16 collision occur.
-- · Ensures back-off functionality is working properly.
-- · Ensures that transmit buffer descriptor is written back with 
--   correct data. (Bit  29 should be set in word 1 indicating the 
--   retry limit was exceeded)
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- 1. Enable GEM for 100-mode operation and transmitting frames.
--
--    Test 1: 16 collisions during transmission
--
-- 2. Set retry test bit to speed up backoff count (bit 12 in network configuration register).
-- 3. Queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 1).  Therefore, the 
--    rest of preamble and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 4. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 2).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 5. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 3).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 6. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 4).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 7. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 5).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 8. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 6).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 9. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--    However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 7).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--    and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 10. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 8).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 11. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 9).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 12. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 10).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 13. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision11).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 14. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 12).  Therefore, the rest of preamble
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 15. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 13).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 16. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 14).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 17. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision115).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 18. After some back-off period, queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame. 
--     However, a collision is detected during preamble (collision 16).  Therefore, the rest of preamble 
--     and SFD should be transmitted. Then, a 32-bit jam sequence should be transmitted.
-- 19. The GEM should now stop trying to re-transmit the frame and write back to the original transmit
--      buffer descriptor indicating that excessive retries  (bit 29) have occurred.
--
-- Test 2: 15 collisions during transmission
--
-- 20. Enable transmit again because tx_go bit was reset because too many retries occurred.
-- 21. Queue up three 8-byte buffers. Then, start transmitting the frame.  However, a collision
